# "If you cast a spell this way, that creature enters with a finality counter on it" is about that spell alone (CR 614.1c,
# 400.7). Faithless Looting discards Hovermyr (1/2) on turn 1 and Leonardo comes down for Black Lotus and a Plains. On turn 3
# Bot1 casts Hovermyr from the graveyard with Leonardo's permission and, holding priority, flashes in Cathar Commando from hand
# on top of it: the Commando resolves first and enters with no finality counter while the Hovermyr spell waits below, and then
# Hovermyr enters with one.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Leonardo, Sewer Samurai
Plains
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Faithless Looting
Hovermyr
Plains
Cathar Commando
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Hovermyr; Plains)
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Leonardo, Sewer Samurai.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Graveyard.Hovermyr.Cast(Ability: During your turn)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cathar Commando.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cathar Commando.Counters.Finality = (absent)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cathar Commando.Counters.Finality = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Hovermyr.Counters.Finality = 1
